From bc8ec4a7ffaff9d8519856a439f7bd4042f0c0ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Janota <Roman.Janota@cesnet.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:08:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] notifd FEATURE yang-push on-change subscriptions

Configured RFC 8641 datastore subscriptions with an on-change update
trigger, its dampening period and excluded changes. The validation
rejects an on-change subscription of factory-default, which has no
changes to subscribe to, and a dampening period that does not fit in
milliseconds.

Every receiver has an srsn subscription of its own, started without
sync-on-start. The daemon requests the resync itself whenever a
receiver becomes active and after every resubscribe instead, so a
receiver that reconnects, and one whose subscription was modified,
gets a new baseline, and no change between the snapshot and the SR
subscription is lost.

Upstream: https://github.com/sysrepo/sysrepo/commit/6ddd6e707ec2c5669e55fdd64c8b44013c3243c8
Signed-off-by: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
